\ ==== unison: :unison 1-7, :detune (cents, total span), :spread 0-1 ====

\ Each note plays :unison copies of every operator, detuned evenly across
\ :detune cents (a span of 20 puts three copies at -10, 0 and +10) and
\ panned evenly across +/- :spread around the patch's :pan. The copies share
\ the operator envelopes; the sum is scaled by 1/sqrt(:unison) so the level
\ of the uncorrelated copies stays close to one voice's.

11 seed

: amp ( v hz -- a ) 48000 swap amplitude-at 0.70710678 / 1000 * round 1000 / ;
: cents ( hz c -- hz' ) 1200 / 2 swap ^ * ;
: left ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 0 1 submatrix ;
: right ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 1 2 submatrix ;
: rms ( v -- r ) dup * mean sqrt ;
: sounding ( patch -- stereo ) silence 0 patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 2 render-audio ;

\ === :unison 1 is the plain voice ===
{ :unison 1 :detune 50 :spread 1 } sounding { } sounding = . cr        \ 1
clear

\ === three copies at -10, 0 and +10 cents ===
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :unison 3 :detune 20 } sounding left to three
three 1000 -10 cents amp . three 1000 amp . three 1000 10 cents amp . cr   \ 0.577 0.577 0.577 (each 1/sqrt 3)
three 1000 -5 cents amp 0.1 < . cr                                        \ 1 (nothing between the copies)
clear

\ === :spread places the copies; 0 keeps left and right identical ===
{ :unison 3 :detune 20 :spread 1 } sounding to wide
wide left wide right = . cr                                    \ 0
{ :unison 3 :detune 20 :spread 0 } sounding to narrow
narrow left narrow right = . cr                                \ 1
{ :operators [ { :fixed 1000 } ] :unison 3 :detune 20 :spread 1 } sounding to fanned
fanned left 1000 -10 cents amp 0 + . fanned right 1000 -10 cents amp 0 + . cr   \ 0.817 0 (the lowest copy hard left: 1/sqrt 3 x sqrt 2)
clear

\ === the level barely moves with the count ===
{ } sounding left rms to one
{ :unison 5 :detune 30 } sounding left rms one / log10 20 * abs 1 < . cr   \ 1 (within 1 dB)
silence clear

\ errors
{ :unison 0 } 0 patch!                                         \ (below 1)
{ :unison 8 } 0 patch!                                         \ (above 7)
{ :unison 2.5 } 0 patch!                                       \ (not an integer)
{ :detune 101 } 0 patch!                                       \ (over 100 cents)
{ :spread 2 } 0 patch!                                         \ (above 1)
